 not appropriate, and there are protections in place.\'\n\n**5. Address the psychological component**:\n\'I also want to talk about how you are feeling emotionally. Your ACL-RSI score tells me you have significant fear about returning, and that is completely normal. Research shows that athletes who return before they are psychologically ready are at higher risk of re-injury. I want to connect you with a sports psychologist who specializes in working with injured athletes. This is not about mental weakness — elite athletes use sports psychology as a performance tool.\'\n\n**6. Provide a realistic and hopeful timeline**:\n\'Based on where you are now at 7 months, I am optimistic about your recovery. If we continue on this trajectory, we can target functional testing at 9 months and, if you pass all criteria, a graduated return to full competition between 9 and 12 months. That gives us a clear goal to work toward together.\'\n\n**Key principles demonstrated**: Unwavering patient advocacy, refusal to compromise medical safety under external pressure, addressing financial/scholarship concerns with concrete institutional resources, psychological support referral, inter-provider communication, empowerment through knowledge.',
